@@ -1592,6 +1592,12 @@ calibration (modem-hrc7000.md 10.4).
 
 ## Receive past the rated bands
 
-16-65, 174-400 and 480-1120 MHz: receive only in FM, while **Tools > RX past bands** is On ([radio-features.md](radio-features.md) 6.2). The option is Off on a first start and after a factory reset; the saved choice survives a restart. Through 740 MHz this follows the FD6818 band table (8.3). The 740-1120 MHz extension is experimental: it reuses the top band-select words, whose row also ends at 1120 MHz in the related FD6818SH driver, but no sensitivity, synthesizer lock or real reception has been measured on a DM-32UV.
+16-65, 174-400 and 480-1120 MHz are receive-only ranges while **Tools > RX past bands** is On
+([radio-features.md](radio-features.md) 6.2). The option is Off on first start and after a factory reset. The saved
+choice survives a restart. The 222-225 MHz band falls inside 174-400 MHz. Enter `222500` in the VFO for 222.500 MHz.
+Receiver sensitivity in this band has yet to be measured. Through 740 MHz the ranges follow the FD6818 band table
+(8.3). The 740-1120 MHz extension is experimental and reuses the top band-select words, whose row also ends at
+1120 MHz in the related FD6818SH driver. Sensitivity, synthesizer lock and reception above 740 MHz have yet to be
+measured on a DM-32UV.
 
 The VFO accepts nine digits above 1 GHz (`112000000` = 1120.00000 MHz); existing entries of up to eight digits keep their 3+5 MHz/decimal meaning. Channel records hold a GHz frequency too, the top nibble of the frequency word a 0xA/0xB marker over seven BCD digits rather than eight (`open-firmware-cps.md` 7.3.3): a build without it reads the record as malformed and skips the channel instead of tuning another frequency. Every mode receives there; PTT remains denied throughout every receive-only extension.
